    "field": "Evaluation of precipitation data sets",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the considerable uncertainty and inconsistency among widely used gridded precipitation datasets in representing extreme events, a problem stemming from varied source data, methodologies, and complex terrain, which complicates the evaluation and reliability of these products.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a method using tail dependence from multivariate extreme value theory to evaluate the consistency of precipitation extremes in different gridded products by performing pairwise comparisons of their joint tail probability distributions.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate the consistency of extreme precipitation events among various gridded observational data sets for the conterminous United States by comparing them pairwise using methods from multivariate extreme value theory, without defining a single \"ground truth\" product.",
    "model": [
        "CESM",
        "CAM5.1"
    ],
